==Strategy==
This stage is essentially [[Choco Highlands]] reborn, except with the two new R.Ost variants released after that stage's debut, Ostromeda and Oldstrich, making their appearance here.

This stage is extremely annoying and cash tight given that Ostromeda spawns extremely quickly followed by an Oldstrich, as well as the lack of actual money supplies other than Doge Dark. Once both ostriches join the fight, it is really hard to stall them outside of Ubers or [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Nova]], meaning that your highest priority is killing Ostromeda as fast as you can. To this end, bring strong backliner units like [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] in order to kill it fast, or even [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] given the high amount of health Ostromeda has. [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] is excellent on this stage given that he can cover for Nova's downtime and even Slow Oldstrich if you got his Talent, while you should make sure to run specialized meatshields like [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] or [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack]] alongside [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]], as well as [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] for the Oldstrich later on. The peons in this stage are also a serious threat, so you can use units with piercing range like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], [[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Macho Legs Cat]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]].

